From 680903a5fedc99bf020a9b64a3c87c81d63d2c85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:55:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Track anchor baselines per child so hidden children and
 pre-map resizes are not lost

Each anchored child remembers the container client size its bounds correspond to, instead of one baseline per container. A window enlarged before its first real allocation (Load, before Show, Shown) now moves anchored children, a child hidden during a resize catches up when shown, and the content-fit/titlebar growth is absorbed by rebasing instead of forgetting the baseline.
